  "current_quotes": 64,
  "summary": "Salad rents idle consumer GPUs and publishes a rate per card for each of four priority tiers. Its pricing page draws the table with a script, and the figures come from the file that page loads - open to anyone, no key and no account - so the link goes to the page where you can see them. High priority is never preempted by other workloads and is shown here as on-demand; Medium, Low and Lowest may be preempted, and are shown as spot. The price covers the GPU with the vCPU and memory the page says are included. Not shown: CPU-only groups, and reserved and volume deals, which publish no rate.",
  "notes": "static salad.com/js/pricing.js (keyless), the file /pricing/ loads to fill its own empty table: a literal of [name, VRAM, High, Medium, Low, Lowest] per GPU class, in the order the table head prints. Four quotes per card, the tier in region; High is on_demand (\"Never preempted by other workloads\"), Medium/Low/Lowest spot (\"May be preempted\"); market community, scope instance (the page states vCPU and RAM are included with every GPU). Not read: CPU-only container groups, Salad Dedicated (reserved, quoted per term), volume and Private Cloud (talk to sales), and the portal classes advertised \"from $0.015 per GPU-hour\", which is a floor for an unnamed set. Raises if the SALAD_GPU_PRICES marker is gone, if no row is priced, or if the tiers are not in High-to-Lowest order, the rates being read by position.",
  "page": "https://gpueconomy.com/providers/salad",
  "referral_url": null,
  "fees": [],
  "slug": "ext-salad",
  "cards": [
   "RTX 4090",
   "RTX 5090"
  ]
 },
